<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dakar (Senegal)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dakar is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cap-vert">Cap-Vert</a> peninsula and the capital of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>. It was the headquarters of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, one of the two great federations through which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> governed its African colonies. It became the capital of independent Senegal in 1960.</p></div>
